# DataShield Project Rules for Cursor / AI Assistants

You are assisting on "DataShield: Django Privacy & Compliance Platform".
Topic: Personal Data Protection & Decree 13/2023 / GDPR Compliance in Django.
Team: Le Duy Khanh (Team Lead), Nguyen Van Hieu (Member).

CRITICAL INSTRUCTIONS:
1. ALWAYS read and inspect existing code in `privacy/models.py`, `privacy/services.py`, `privacy/views.py`, and `config/settings.py` before modifying or proposing code.
2. NEVER bypass PostgreSQL Row-Level Security (RLS) or `TenantScopedModel`.
3. NEVER allow mutation or deletion of `AuditEvent` (it is an immutable SHA-256 hash ledger).
4. Strictly follow Python 3.12+ type annotations and clean architecture.
5. All sensitive data must adhere to Decree 13/2023/ND-CP and GDPR privacy requirements.
6. Ensure existing tests pass via `pytest`.
